# Version control and CI
.git
.github

# Claude Code settings
.claude

# Helm charts — not needed by most image builds. Exception: Dockerfile.test
# needs charts/scoreboard (+ its local file://../falco-ctf-common chart
# dependency, P21 item 5) to `helm template`
# charts/scoreboard/templates/ingress-journey.yaml for the ADR-0021 (Issue
# #238, Hard Invariant I15) ingress-participant-route-coverage test. Every
# OTHER Dockerfile using this root context (scoreboard/auth-policy/
# collector image builds, Dockerfile.gen, Dockerfile.tidy) never COPYs
# charts/ regardless of what's in the build context, so widening the
# context here doesn't change what lands in any final image layer.
#
# `charts/*` (exclude each DIRECT child) + `!charts/<name>/` (re-include
# specific children) is the standard "exclude everything except these"
# idiom — NOT the same as excluding `charts/` itself and trying to
# re-include a file nested inside it, which .dockerignore/.gitignore
# semantics do NOT support (a negation cannot resurrect a path under an
# already fully-excluded parent). Re-including the directory ENTRY itself
# via `charts/*` + `!charts/scoreboard/` is the supported form: once
# re-included, nothing further excludes its own contents.
charts/*
!charts/scoreboard/
!charts/falco-ctf-common/

# Scan output
scan-logs/

# Secrets and local state
*.db
.env
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
